WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.110
The Monaco Cup semifinals.

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:10.490
With a sports bread made of eel, black beans, nori and silk powder, he surpassed even Kayser.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:14.580
The Japanese representatives are going to the finals!

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.990
We did it Suwabara!

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.290
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.210
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.460
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.980
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:34.100
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.070
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.400
A menace that exceeds the speed of sound!!

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.700
<i>Gopan</i> #97!

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:16.990
Cheers!

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.240
Congratulations on getting into the finals!

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.450
It’s amazing that you could defeat <i>that</i> Kayser.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.590
I was worried in the beginning, but...

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:30.460
having defeated Kayser, we’re really the best.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:35.180
With this, customers will start
returning to my store a little as well.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:36.850
Everything is thanks to you guys.

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.100
So eat up.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.100
Oh, you don’t have to do that.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.930
Thank you, Kazuma, Kai.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.900
It was amazing, Azuma and Suwabara.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.180
A toast to the both of you.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.620
This time, I didn’t do anything.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.580
Everything is thanks to Azuma.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:00.030
That’s not true!

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:01.530
Azuma...

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:10.750
I just happened to see on TV once
that silk powder is good for your body.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:14.590
So, I made <i>Japan</i> #51 for my sister,
who was on the track team in university.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:18.800
At that time, I just added garlic to it
since I’d heard it was good for stamina.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.520
This time I had to make bread for
F1 racers who overuse their eyes.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:27.400
But, without Suwabara’s help, I
wouldn’t even have thought of using eel,

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:31.910
nori and black soy beans, which are
good for your eyes, instead of garlic.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:39.030
But Azuma, how did you know that
black soy beans have anthocyanin in them?

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:43.910
That’s because my grandfather always boasts that he

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:48.040
still has perfect vision thanks to
eating black soy beans everyday.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:52.960
Oh, there’s a lion 5km ahead, Kazuma!

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.850
Not possible. This is Japan after all.

00:03:58.390 --> 00:03:58.630
Restoration and reforms are
necessary to rebuild our economy!

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:01.050
Meeting to discuss earnest politics.
Koiizumi Junichirou

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:01.510
Restoration and reforms are
necessary to rebuild our economy!

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.550
So I was sure that it’s a good food for your eyes.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.060
I see.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.810
So, it was your naivete in
believing the nonsense of an old man

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.610
who couldn’t even distinguish
between a human being and a lion...

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:14.310
that helped make the bread this time.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:18.020
I wonder why he can’t praise him normally...?

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:21.240
But, now that we’ve come
this far, it’s an easy win, right?

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:25.950
After all, we even defeated the Kaysers.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:29.920
And in the end, the American team just has Shachihoko.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:33.040
So we couldn’t possibly lose.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.040
V for Victory!

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:39.130
But, it’s not you who defeated the Kaysers.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:40.390
I wonder...

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:45.560
Unlike you guys, who went
home straight after your match,

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:48.850
I stayed behind to watch the
semifinals between America and China.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.850
And the winners are... them.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.980
All three of America’s breads won.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.890
China lost completely.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.660
That’s probably because China was just too weak.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.530
I don’t think Shachihoko is weak, but...

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.330
he’s not an opponent we’d
lose to with Azuma on our side.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.290
Right, Azuma-chan?

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:06.790
Ow. Ouch.
Right, Azuma-chan?

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:07.660
Ow. Ouch.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:08.160
Why are you pulling it?

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.410
Oh, sorry. Sorry.
Why are you pulling it?

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:13.140
Will you still take it easy after hearing that

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:16.920
Shachihoko’s bread placed third in the semifinals?

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.850
What was that?!

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.420
Then, who placed first?

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.430
That inconspicuous stooped guy.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:25.420
His name is Shadow.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.770
I wonder who he is...

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:32.100
He didn’t look like he was doing
particularly well in the matches so far.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.940
To think he’s that skilled...

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:36.690
Even I don’t know that.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:44.870
But, his <i>Gopan</i> #97 has the potential to surpass even Azuma’s <i>Japan</i> #51.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.950
G-<i>Gopan</i> #97?

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:48.950
Yeah.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:54.000
Like its name suggests, the bread is
made with rice flour instead of wheat flour.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:59.380
And it seems that he used black
currants as a good ingredient for your eyes.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:02.970
For muscle reinforcement, he added in protein.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:05.390
Black currants in rice?

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:08.220
It doesn’t seem like a particularly delicious bread...

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.430
If you think about it the usual way.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:15.150
But, in order for the taste to remain
unaffected, he processed it scientifically.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:19.440
It seems that he only mixed in the active
ingredients of black currants and protein.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:25.070
For flavoring, he added in
consomme, saffron and seafood as a base.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.450
In the end, he baked it to seem like paella.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:28.950
Sounds awesome.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:33.700
Seems like things have
turned problematic again, Azuma.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:37.500
It’s not as problematic as your wig,
so don’t worry, Kawachi.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.210
You’re going to make fun of it
at this point in time?

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:43.930
Actually, I was thinking the same thing.

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:45.710
That that’s just <i>bad</i>.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.220
Sorry. Me, too.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:50.720
Secretly, I was thinking so as well.

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:56.100
Don’t get so down, Kawachi.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.770
I’ll do my best.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:01.400
I won’t lose to someone like the American representatives.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:04.700
But, it has nothing to do with my slipped wig!

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:07.070
Whatever, do what you want.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.700
I will no longer step forward.

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.490
I’ll leave everything to Azuma.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.000
Hey, Kawachi!

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.330
Don’t you want to win?

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.170
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:16.920
Of course I want to!

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:20.710
But, I don’t want to embarrass
myself anymore in front of people.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:24.090
And with Azuma here, we have
nothing to worry about, right?

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:25.710
That’s not good enough.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.550
After all, the finals consist of man-to-man battles.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.390
A battle with no ties.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.350
The first team to win twice is the victor.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:40.440
Therefore, Azuma’s match and Kawachi’s match have the same value.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.280
Make sure to understand that.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:44.950
F-For real?!

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:54.580
First, let me congratulate you on making it to the finals.

00:07:54.580 --> 00:08:00.630
Would you like some champagne,
Shadow-kun?

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:03.040
Anyway...

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:10.800
Just be careful of Japan’s Azuma-kun.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:19.780
Even though my <i>Gopan</i> might be the best, we can’t get too confident.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:28.120
Keep the copying to just the bread!

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:32.070
Keep the copying to just the bread!

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:42.670
The sound in the F1 is pretty amazing, too.

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:44.170
My eardrums feel like they might burst.

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:47.380
They’re going really fast even though it’s just free runs they’re doing prior to the finals...

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:52.180
The impact is really different
from when you’re seeing it on TV.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:55.220
Oh! Isn’t that Mikhail Schukapper?

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:56.100
A Kappa?!

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.770
Don’t you know?!

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.050
He’s been the world champion five times in a row

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:02.110
and has been getting the best records in the world.

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:06.120
He’s an F1 racer who wants to be
known as the best racer in the world.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:10.070
In yesterday’s semis, he was in the pole position.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:14.500
As the “Emperor” of the F1, he’s expected to win the Monaco Grand Prix as well.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.610
That Kappa dude is that amazing?!

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:22.160
That amazing man is going to be eating your bread.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.790
There’s no honor greater than this as a baker.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.340
If you don’t show more happiness about it,
you’ll be getting some divine punishment.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:29.960
Yay! Yay! Yay!

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.090
They seem really happy.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:36.400
Compared to them, what’s wrong with you, Ryou?

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.350
I’m worried.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:40.230
Worried?

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:44.270
Shadow’s and Azuma’s breads
won first place in the semifinals.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:47.650
And they’re being assessed by having that Schukapper eat it.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:53.990
If Schukapper likes Shadow’s <i>Gopan</i> better
than <i>Japan</i>, what do you think will happen?

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.240
What do you mean, what will happen?

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:59.450
As far as I know, Azuma
has never lost in a bread battle.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:02.170
But, when such geniuses lose for the first time,

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:06.750
they get hurt and may never be able to get back on their feet.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:09.460
I’m worried about that.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.000
Ryou...

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.800
Attention, attention.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.380
Will the creators of the breads that won first place in the semifinals

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:19.270
please proceed to the kitchen.

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:22.560
Azuma and Shadow,
I’m talking about you guys.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.220
Oh, I should get going.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.660
Good luck.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:27.230
Go.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:28.820
Yep!

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:31.990
Hey guys!

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:34.370
There’s something I want to discuss.

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:41.240
Umm... I wonder where the kitchen is...?

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.380
It’s not like I don’t understand your worrying, but...

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:50.000
it isn’t a given that Azuma is going to lose.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.840
Yeah, Kuro-yan.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:58.220
While you might say that <i>Gopan</i> #97 will
beat <i>Japan</i> #51, it’s just a possibility, right?

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:00.350
It’s <i>Japan</i> #51 Kai.

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:02.260
Don’t forget the Kai. The Kai.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:09.980
No, I think the <i>Japan</i> #51 Kai
will lose to the <i>Gopan</i> #97, 100%.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.230
What was that?!

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.200
Goal!

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:20.910
The champion just came in,
and it’s Mikhail Schukapper!

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:23.050
Another easy win!!

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:38.470
Schukapper-san. Congratulations on your win.

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:40.600
Thank you, sara sara.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:43.850
This is your 100th consecutive win!

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:45.440
Thank you, sara sara.

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:48.020
It’s thanks to my fans out there, sara.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:51.940
And, I tend to play a lot of pranks.

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:58.370
So, I thank my friends and parents in Tongara
for forgiving a prankster like me, sara. Kappa!

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:06.370
I used to challenge the mountain paths
with our store’s car when I was young.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:10.380
The trick was to drive the car
without spilling the water and tofu.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:13.370
I’m not really asking for these details...

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:17.510
Note: Hashiriya = street racer
Schukapper was a hashiriya in the past, huh?

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:19.640
But, does Germany even have tofu?

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:20.810
Paella.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:27.940
I told you the <i>Gopan</i> #97 was
flavored to seem like paella, right?

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:29.860
Yeah, I believe so...

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:30.890
What about it?

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:33.910
Hashiriya.

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:35.110
Ha-shi-ri-ya.

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:36.570
Pa-e-ri-ya.

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:37.400
Don’t tell me...

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:42.830
But, it’s pretty cool that you were a hashiriya.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:46.870
It wasn’t really anything particularly cool.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:52.040
I was really good at driving and playing pranks, but I was a coward and a weakling.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.090
Huh?

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:57.420
Why am I unable to stop myself from
talking about my embarrassing past, sara?

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:02.420
When I was 15, Schwienrich-kun from Class 3-B would always...

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:04.350
Hey, Kapper.

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:06.470
Go to the neighboring village to buy bread.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:07.810
Be back in 5 minutes.

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:09.180
O-Okay, sara!

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:13.900
I got it.

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:15.030
You idiot!

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:16.150
You’re 5 seconds late.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.980
You plan on letting me starve to death?!

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:20.230
Pashiriya!

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.620
Now that I think about it,

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:29.250
it’s thanks to Schwienrich’s training that my driving technique got so good, sara.

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:32.130
Is... Is that so?

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:35.880
By the way, that’s a pretty embarrassing past, right?

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:39.330
Why did you let the cat out of the bag here?

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:43.340
It’s due to the deliciousness of
the bread I was fed before the finals.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:45.310
There were two types of bread.

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:47.060
Both of them had strange names.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:50.550
One was <i>Japan</i>. The other was <i>Gopan</i>.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:53.480
Both were great breads, sara.

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:58.060
Even in my fatherland Germany,
I’ve never tasted a bread so delicious!

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:00.320
Especially the <i>Gopan</i>.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:04.820
That was deliciousness suitable to
become the world champion of breads.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.550
Wait, Kawachi.

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:17.920
Leave him be.

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.010
But!

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:25.390
Accepting the cruel truth before him and seeing
whether or not he can overcome it is up to him.

00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:27.510
It’s not a matter that others can say anything about.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:31.480
And I don’t think that a human being who’s been a loser at everything since birth

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:36.740
can comfort the wounds of a genius who’s lost at something for the first time since birth.

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:38.870
Kuro-yan...

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.020
Who you calling a loser of a human being?!

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:43.780
Right?

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:44.530
Right.

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:46.290
Yeah...

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:53.760
Shadow, wait a moment please.

00:15:02.590 --> 00:15:04.800
Azuma isn’t back yet?

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:05.970
Nope.

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:09.060
I guess it really was a shock to him.

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:12.810
We might have to assume the worst.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:15.010
What do you mean, the worst?

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:18.520
In his despair, he might commit sui–

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:22.110
Don’t even say that!

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:25.530
Aren’t you exaggerating a bit much for just one loss?

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:28.660
But, it’s already this late.

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:32.950
He’s not familiar with the local area
and might be lost and lonely.

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:35.080
We left him alone for too long.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:37.540
I’m going to look for him.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.790
Let’s split up and search in places he might be at.

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:41.260
Yeah.

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:50.890
Say, Shadow.

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:58.010
I just wanted to thank you.

00:15:58.270 --> 00:15:59.230
Geez!

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:03.280
Would you just stop imitating me and have a decent conversation instead?!

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:07.480
If not, I can’t go home even if I want to.

00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:11.240
Yeah, that’s true.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:16.000
After all, imitating you wouldn’t
make me the best in the world.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:29.380
You really made us all worry.

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:33.380
We’d been searching for you until morning.

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:39.900
But, it’s not my fault.

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:42.610
Last night, I went to meet that Shadow guy.

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:44.990
He just kept imitating me.

00:16:44.990 --> 00:16:46.610
It’s because of that.

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.480
Huh? Imitating you?

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:49.440
What are you talking about?

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:51.620
Like I said. Imitating.

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:55.160
He imitated everything, from
the things I’d say to my gestures...

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.000
That’s why I got stubborn, too.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:00.750
And I tried poses that he couldn’t possibly imitate.

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:03.710
But he copied them all perfectly.

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:06.420
That really, really annoyed me.

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.920
And before I realized it, it was the middle of the night.

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:10.920
Imitations?

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:12.600
What the hell is that?

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:16.270
If you’re going to lie, then say something believable.

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:18.270
I-It’s the truth I tell you.

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:22.430
So, what exactly did you
want to talk to that mimic about?

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:25.940
I wanted to thank him.

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:27.440
Thank him?

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:31.620
I can’t find the kitchen...

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:33.240
Azuma!

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:34.440
Over here.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:36.700
Good luck to the both of you.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:37.450
Yep!

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:47.540
I saw Shadow kneading the flour with an expertise that

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:50.930
made it hard to believe that he was a young baker.

00:17:50.930 --> 00:17:56.880
I’ve seen bakers with great expertise,
like Manager and Old Man Mokoyama.

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.590
And, he was on par with them.

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:02.640
No, he appeared better than them.

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:08.610
His movements were clearly those of a veteran baker.

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:12.360
It’s certain that he’s practiced hard day after day.

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:19.120
When I saw that, I felt that I must work harder, too.

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:21.570
That’s why I wanted to thank him.

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:23.830
I see.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:27.620
So, you didn’t feel the slightest
shock upon losing to Shadow, huh?

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:29.380
Shock upon losing?

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:30.620
What are you talking about?

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:35.760
Either way.

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:37.680
I’m glad that you’re all right.

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:41.760
In one hour, the theme of the finals will be announced by Pierrot.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:44.350
Do whatever you like until then.

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:45.850
Huh?

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.850
Geez.

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:55.120
I guess it means that people with real
ambitions and dreams don’t break easily.

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:02.370
It looks like you finally made it to the finals.

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:06.500
With this and that, I’ll announce the final theme.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:11.880
As you all know, the finals consist
of three direct man-to-man matches.

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.630
Therefore, there are three themes.

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:17.630
In other words, the clothing, food and shelter of bread.

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:18.430
Clothing?

00:19:18.430 --> 00:19:19.180
Food?

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:20.130
Shelter?

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.810
What’s that supposed to mean?

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:22.560
There, there.

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:25.650
I’ll explain, so don’t panic.

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:27.640
Starting with the theme of the first match.

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:28.980
Clothing!

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:31.820
Make your bread beautiful like the things people wear.

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:35.150
This is a match to see who
can mold a more beautiful bread.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:37.150
Next, the second match.

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:38.910
Food!

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:43.660
This is a match to make a dinner bread, suitable to eat everyday.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:46.410
And the theme for the third match.

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:47.750
Shelter!

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:49.590
That bread should have the taste of your homeland.

00:19:49.590 --> 00:19:54.130
A match where you make bread that
best expresses the taste of your homeland.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:59.010
It goes without saying that making bread
which tastes good is an absolute requirement.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:04.140
Input that into your heads and
please make a bread suitable for the finals.

00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:05.850
I see.

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.650
Yeah, I see...

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:11.640
And by the way, it matters not which combatant chooses which theme.

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:18.150
Please note that should you lose twice in
a row, the third match will not take place.

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:21.990
The choice of combatants should
be submitted by tomorrow morning.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:25.410
Once your choice is made, it cannot be changed at a later point.

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:31.090
Both countries should probably devise a
plan by using each combatant’s specialty.

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:32.410
That’s all.

00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:36.300
Looks like it’s finally time, right Azuma?

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:37.070
Yep.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:41.920
After placing third in the
semifinals, though, I can’t hope too much.

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:47.430
I may not even be able to fight Azuma.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:52.390
But, let’s both fight it out fair
and square, shall we, Azuma?

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:55.580
Yep. Of course!

00:20:57.860 --> 00:21:00.990
The owner Kirisaki... and Shachihoko.

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:05.700
For some reason, both of them
seem really interested in this kid.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:10.450
But he hasn’t left me with an impression
of being anything more than a regular idiot.

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:20.340
Since it’s about the taste of your homeland,
the third match should go to Azuma.

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:22.100
He’s the guy with the <i>Japan</i> after all.

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:26.510
But, should you have already
lost twice, then Japan is done for.

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:28.440
Baldy might lose, but...

00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:32.190
even should the Earth revolve in the opposite direction, I can’t possibly lose.

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:33.520
So, don’t worry.

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:34.730
Wait just a moment, you asshole.

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:37.940
Then, we’ll have Kazuma in the third match.

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:39.690
Which one will the two of you take?

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:41.990
Uh... hahaha.

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:46.660
Well, I’ve never really gotten higher than a 2 in art...

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:49.780
So, fighting over the molding of bread might be a little...

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:52.950
Only in art?

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:58.220
Other than that, I’d always get
comments about not settling well in class...

00:21:58.220 --> 00:21:59.210
Kawachi.

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:00.710
Fine then.

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:07.770
The real warrior shows the best swordsmanship without needing to choose his sword.

00:22:07.770 --> 00:22:11.270
And he stands on the front
lines of the battle to spearhead it.

00:22:11.270 --> 00:22:13.680
I will take on the first match.

00:22:14.110 --> 00:22:15.360
All right.

00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:16.400
It’s decided then.

00:22:17.070 --> 00:22:20.900
The theme of the first match,
a well-molded bread, goes to Suwabara.

00:22:21.490 --> 00:22:24.900
The theme of the second match,
dinner bread, goes to Kawachi.

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:29.910
The theme of the third match, a bread with
the taste of your homeland, goes to Azuma.

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:31.580
Let’s aim to win!

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:33.420
All right!

00:24:06.260 --> 00:24:07.720
I will cut down the first opponent.

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:09.430
No matter who it is, I won’t hold back.

00:24:09.430 --> 00:24:12.040
The opponent is the winner of
the world pastry tournament.

00:24:12.040 --> 00:24:13.190
And for some reason, she’s in a swimsuit.

00:24:13.190 --> 00:24:15.130
What was that?!

00:24:15.130 --> 00:24:16.100
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.100 --> 00:24:17.190
Naked, naked, naked!!

00:24:17.190 --> 00:24:17.270
The magnificent bread match!

00:24:17.270 --> 00:24:18.880
The magnificent bread match!
Naked, naked, naked!!

00:24:18.880 --> 00:24:19.860
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.380 --> 00:24:22.610
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.220 --> 00:24:25.090
The jet-black black soy beans.

00:24:25.090 --> 00:24:27.220
They are very rich in anthocyanin.

00:24:27.220 --> 00:24:30.010
So, in addition to improving your eyesight,
it helps with blood flow

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:31.630
and reduction of your body fat.

00:24:32.270 --> 00:24:34.000
Oh?!
